  "_comment": "The pier ramp: straight up from the quay onto the high pier, steep enough to feel it, over a crest at the top and into a turn banked hard round the end of the pier, then over the start road, across the moving crane decks, down the banked switchbacks to the water and a dip along the waterfront, an off-camber quay and a glide home. Hit the crane switch and the container yard opens a way through the stacks, where the cranes lower containers one side and then the other; the tide creeps over the waterfront from lap 2, and on the last lap containers land on the pier.",
